title: "Auto-SOF: automated surrogate-based multi-objective optimization framework"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alirezza18/nepenthe-auto-sof"
type: software
keywords:
  - surrogate modeling
  - multi-objective optimization
  - NSGA-II
  - NSGA-III
  - machine learning
  - simulation-driven design
  - streamlit
abstract: >-
  Auto-SOF is a no-code, six-step Streamlit workspace that automates the
  surrogate-based optimization loop used in simulation-driven design: it fits
  21 cross-validated regression models (including hybrid stacked ensembles
  with out-of-fold meta-learning), runs ten optimizers (from-scratch NSGA-II,
  NSGA-III, Steady-State NSGA-II, HypE, and surrogate-assisted loops), and
  returns Pareto-optimal designs as a decision package. Reproducibility is
  explicit: every solver draws randomness from a local seed, and sessions are
  portable as a single project file.
